# Agent Security Rules

Spec: AgentSecurityRules
Purpose:
  Define how ECC AgentShield security patterns map to SDD security
  control levels (L0-L5). Integration point between ECC's 102 static rules
  and SDD's security enforcement pipeline.

Owns: agent/security-rules.sdd

AgentShieldMapping:
  AgentShieldRules: 102
  AgentShieldTests: 1,282
  Coverage: 98%

  FiveCategories:
    1. Secrets Detection:
       patterns: 14
       mapped_to: PAT_SECRET_* in @../security/controls.sdd
       sdd_level: L2
       examples:
         - hardcoded API keys
         - hardcoded database credentials
         - hardcoded tokens
       sdd_integration:
         - PostToolUse[Edit/Write] hook checks
         - PreCommit check
         - R1 review gate

    2. Permission Auditing:
       mapped_to: AG1-AG10 in @INDEX.sdd
       sdd_level: L3
       checks:
         - tool allowlist over-grants
         - path access too broad
         - agent config permissions
       sdd_integration:
         - Agent capabilities must match role definition (@roles.sdd)
         - Tool allowlist enforced at @permissions.sdd
         - Permission changes require @approvals.sdd

    3. Hook Injection Analysis:
       mapped_to: ADAPTER1-ADAPTER15 in @../runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd
       sdd_level: L4
       checks:
         - hooks can be exploited to run arbitrary commands
         - hook injection vectors in agent configs
       sdd_integration:
         - HookBridge validates all hook inputs
         - PostToolUse hooks sanitize before processing
         - ENFORCE mode blocks on L4 patterns

    4. MCP Server Risk Profiling:
       mapped_to: mcp-integration.sdd MCPBridge
       sdd_level: L3-L4 (contextual)
       checks:
         - what each MCP server can read, write, or call
         - exposure surface analysis
         - cross-server chaining risks
       sdd_integration:
         - Only allowlisted MCP servers permitted (@mcp-integration.sdd)
         - Server connections version-pinned (not @latest)
         - Graceful degradation if server unavailable

    5. Agent Config Review:
       mapped_to: AG1-AG10 in @agent/INDEX.sdd
       sdd_level: L2-L5 (contextual)
       checks:
         - prompt injection vectors
         - tool allowlist over-grants
         - missing constraints
       sdd_integration:
         - All agent configs validated against @roles.sdd
         - Constraints must match role capabilities
         - Missing constraints flagged as L2 finding

SecurityEnforcement:
  Modes:
    OBSERVE:
      description: warnings logged, tool proceeds, OBS emitted
      triggers: L1-L3 patterns, non-critical findings
      output: OBS12 security_gate_warned

    ENFORCE:
      description: blocks tool call on security violation
      triggers: L4-L5 patterns, critical findings (grade F)
      output: exit 2 + OBS13 security_gate_blocked

  LLevelMapping:
    L0: No security controls — not recommended for any project
    L1: Basic scanning — secrets detection only (grade C minimum)
    L2: Standard review — secrets + basic permission audit (grade B minimum)
    L3: Enhanced review — adds hook injection + MCP risk (grade A minimum)
    L4: Full audit — all 5 AgentShield categories (grade A+ required)
    L5: Paranoid mode — adversarial review with -opus flag

  Default:
    project_level_L1: OBSERVE for secrets only
    project_level_L2: OBSERVE L1-L2, ENFORCE L3+
    project_level_L3: OBSERVE L1-L2, ENFORCE L3+
    project_level_L4: ENFORCE L2+ (critical)
    project_level_L5: ENFORCE L1+ (paranoid)

Rules:
  [SEC-01] AgentShield findings MUST be mapped to SDD L-levels before enforcement.
  [SEC-02] Secrets detection (14 patterns) is mandatory at L1+.
  [SEC-03] Agent config review MUST validate against @roles.sdd capabilities.
  [SEC-04] MCP server allowlist MUST be enforced by @../runtime/mcp-integration.sdd.
  [SEC-05] AgentShield scan MUST be invoked at R1 gate for all code changes.
  [SEC-06] Critical findings (grade F) MUST exit with code 2.
  [SEC-07] -fix flag auto-applies only to safe issues (secrets removal, permission tightening).
  [SEC-08] -opus red-team/blue-team pipeline invoked only for L4+ projects.

ScanInvocation:
  manual: npx ecc-agentshield scan
  from_claude: /security-scan
  auto_trigger:
    - PostToolUse[Edit/Write] → secrets + injection scan
    - PreCommit → full AgentShield scan
    - R1 gate → full AgentShield + hook injection scan

Navigation:
  AgentIndex: @INDEX.sdd
  SecurityControls: @../security/controls.sdd
  SecurityLevels: @../security/levels.sdd
  AdapterRuntime: @../runtime/adapter-runtime.sdd
  McpIntegration: @../runtime/mcp-integration.sdd
  AgentRoles: @roles.sdd
  AgentPermissions: @permissions.sdd

State: +
